{
 "schema": "flint.request-allocations/1",
 "description": "Per-request GC allocation budgets of the Phase 1 apps (owner decision 9a9aefa0, work-queue item 28). Each app's test (benchmarks/spring/flint/<app>/test/.../request_allocations_test.d) serves every request of its side-by-side suite (benchmarks/spring/suites/requests/<app>.json) on the real servlet path, on druntime's own collector behind flint.arena's allocation counter, and fails when a request's server-side allocations or bytes exceed its budget, naming the top allocating functions. A budget starts at the measured cost x1.25, rounded up, and only goes down: the structural gate refuses a raise (tools/request_allocation_ratchet.py). 'measured' is the cost recorded with the budget (FLINT_REQUEST_ALLOCATIONS=record prints current costs); lower both as cuts land. gs-rest-service's counts are deterministic and equal on DMD and LDC; petclinic-rest's agree within one allocation and about 1% of bytes across runs and compilers (budgets take the largest of three runs); gs-relational-data-access is a command-line application whose budget is one run.",
